1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,102
What if every bacterium in your body vanished, right now?

2
00:00:03,617 --> 00:00:06,263
You'd lose about thirty-eight trillion cells.

3
00:00:06,263 --> 00:00:07,968
More than your own, by count.

4
00:00:07,968 --> 00:00:10,556
But they only weigh about two hundred grams.

5
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:15,050
Within a day, the cells lining your colon would be low on fuel.

6
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:18,225
They run on butyrate, made by bacteria from fiber.

7
00:00:18,525 --> 00:00:20,846
Like and subscribe for more body what-ifs.

8
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:25,127
In germ-free lab mice, a gut pouch called the cecum balloons.

9
00:00:25,127 --> 00:00:28,347
In some strains, up to a fifth of their body weight.

10
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:30,651
But you couldn't stay sterile.

11
00:00:30,651 --> 00:00:35,632
One person can add around thirty-seven million bacteria to a room's air every hour.

12
00:00:36,117 --> 00:00:37,798
So how long before they're back?

13
00:00:37,798 --> 00:00:39,164
Full story on the channel.
